Source: Polanco, Muller & Krstulovic, "Vortex clustering, polarisation and circulation
        intermittency in classical and quantum turbulence", Nature Communications 12, 7090 (2021);
        dataset supports the circulation-statistics analysis (see also PRX 11, 011053 (2021)).
Record: https://zenodo.org/records/5510351  (concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.5510350)
Licence: CC-BY-4.0, open, no authentication.
Retrieved: 2026-09-20.
Files: ReaPsi.001.dat, ImaPsi.001.dat -- each exactly 134,217,728 bytes = 256^3 * 8.
Format: headerless raw binary, float64 little-endian, COLUMN-MAJOR (Fortran) order.
        psi = Re + i*Im on a 256^3 periodic grid.
        np.fromfile(f, dtype='<f8').reshape(256, 256, 256, order='F')
Physics: instantaneous 3D wavefunction of a GENERALISED (nonlocal, roton-bearing) Gross-Pitaevskii
        simulation of quantum turbulence. NOT a plain weakly-interacting BEC: the model is tuned to
        reproduce a roton in the He-4 dispersion.
Scales:  L = 2*pi periodic, sound speed c = 1, dx = 2*pi/256 = 0.0245437,
         xi = 1.5*dx = 0.0368155, so the box is 170.7 xi.
         SOURCE OF xi: the authors' own analysis code, ParamsGP(dims; L=(2pi,2pi,2pi), c=1.0,
         nxi=1.5) in examples/circulation_GP.jl of github.com/jipolanco/Circulation.jl.
         It is THEIR convention, adopted here, not derived in this repository.
Tier: B (author-published simulation output, exact binary, parameters recoverable).
Used for: workstream T (docs/designs/TDA_VORTEX_FLOOR.md).
Not in file: any in-band metadata. No time series (single snapshot).
